From ffa5f48121ddbc8814d79d76aa1c830d4becfc0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaxdad <atxhxag@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:58:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] feat(egfx): tell a presenting decoder which view it
 gets

`H264Decoder::present` gains a `PresentedView`: an AVC420 picture, or the
main or auxiliary view of an AVC444 update with its layout (AVC444 or
AVC444v2) and, for a main view, whether the auxiliary view of the same
update follows. The auxiliary view now comes with its own region
rectangles instead of none, so a decoder that presents frames can combine
both views into a 4:4:4 picture, or keep showing the main view alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
